The Baliscan '''Secretariat of International Affairs and Cooperation''' ({{lang-bl|Sectretaria d'Asuntos Internacionales y Cooperación}}), '''SAIC''', is the [[Secretariat Council (Balisca)|government department]] responsible for [[Balisca]]'s [[Foreign relations of Balisca|international affairs and relations]]. The International Secretariat is the nationwide department who oversees the international diplomatic action of the Baliscan regions and other administrations as well as overseeing the international actions of the constitutional bodies. In this sense, from the Secretariat depends the [[International Service (Balisca)|International Service]], the set of individuals, bodies and institutions with competence in international matters.

The International Service is composed for more than 250 diplomatic missions around the world, including {{W|embassies}}, {{W|consulates}}, and other facilities.
==Responsibilities==
The Secretariat of International Affairs and Cooperation is a department of the General Administration responsible for:
*Planning, managing, carrying out and evaluating Baliscan international policy and the international cooperation policy for social development and {{W|social progress|progress}}, paying special attention it's relation to the {{W|Global South}}.
*Coordinating and supervising all actions done in this areas by the other Ministries and Public Administrations.
*Advocating for {{W|global justice movement|global justice}} and promoting international {{W|solidarity}}.
*Providing both routine and rapid assistance with [[immigration to Balisca|immigration process]], {{W|refugee}} and {{W|asylum}} services
*Promoting cross-border and interterritorial cooperation.
*Promoting international {{W|social tolerance}} and respect for {{W|human rights}} via the {{W|International Bill of Human Rights}}.
*Protecting Baliscan people abroad through {{W|antimilitarism|non-militaristic}} measures.
*Preparing, negotiating and processing the international treaties which [[Balisca]] is part of.
